{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Declared mutants of HDR and tonemapping (render-pipeline declaration section 16 and its revision 16.8, v8-arch-gyo2-render-a4; 判定 H1 to H6; render RD-4, RD-11, RD-13 to RD-15). One per independently wrong decision (tests/common/mutation/README.md, criteria 1 to 3 and 9). The gh- mutants need a GPU (label gpu, Lavapipe); the shader ones (Tonemapping.hlsli, Color.hlsli, LinearColour.hlsli, tonemapping.frag.hlsl) rebuild the embedded shaders. Retired with revision 16.8: the CPU curves' mutants (tm-reinhard-formula, tm-luminance-weights, tm-aces-fit, tm-boring-curve, tm-pbr-toe, tm-negative-kept, tm-luminance-black: the CPU curves are now the tests' own reference, TonemappingReference.hpp, checked against Bevy's values; the Engine's curves are the shader's, guarded by the gh- ones), the sRGB functions' (tm-encode-*, tm-decode-toe: render uses Math's DecodeSrgb / EncodeSrgb, guarded by math's tests), Exposure's (tm-exposure-*, re-hdr-exposure-ignored: Exposure moved to B4), tm-bytes-alpha (the tests' reference), gh-method-values (one list of values for both sides now, TonemappingMethods.h: a wrong value is the same on both sides), tm-sync-per-camera and re-hdr's per-target picture (a picture per camera now). Not added (with the reason): the shader's negative channels taken as 0 and its black guard (no GPU stimulus is negative or black under that curve); the tonemapping pass's alpha (every stimulus has alpha 1); a picture put in retained (no code names a picture there: camera_render retains targets of source cameras only); the backend's texture flag (GPUTexture::linear) apart from gh-linear-flag-not-pushed (the same wrong flag reaches the shader).",
